<%
  const sections = [
    { id: 'purpose', title: 'Purpose' },
    { id: 'permitted-use', title: 'Permitted use' },
    { id: 'prohibited-use', title: 'Prohibited use' },
    { id: 'resource-responsibility', title: 'Resource responsibility' },
    { id: 'account-rules', title: 'Account rules' },
    { id: 'enforcement', title: 'Enforcement' },
    { id: 'reporting', title: 'Reporting' },
  ];
%>
<%- include('../partials/legal/header') %>

<div class="legal">
  <%- include('../partials/legal/toc', { sections }) %>

  <article class="legal__prose">
    <h2 id="purpose">Purpose</h2>
    <p>HelloDeploy provides a free deployment platform for personal and educational projects. This policy describes what you may and may not deploy. Using HelloDeploy means you accept these rules.</p>

    <h2 id="permitted-use">Permitted use</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Personal web applications and APIs for learning or portfolio purposes.</li>
      <li>Open-source project demos and educational coursework.</li>
      <li>Internal tools used by you and your project team members.</li>
      <li>Any application whose content and behaviour are lawful in your jurisdiction.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="prohibited-use">Prohibited use</h2>
    <p>The following are not allowed on HelloDeploy under any circumstances:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Illegal content.</strong> Anything that violates applicable law, including copyright infringement, child exploitation material, or content that incites violence.</li>
      <li><strong>Malware and exploits.</strong> Applications designed to attack, infect, or compromise other systems or users.</li>
      <li><strong>Phishing and fraud.</strong> Impersonating other services, collecting credentials under false pretences, or conducting scams.</li>
      <li><strong>Cryptocurrency mining.</strong> Using platform resources to mine or generate cryptocurrency.</li>
      <li><strong>Sexually explicit services.</strong> Pornography, explicit adult services, or sexual content of any kind involving minors. Lawful sexual health, medical, and educational information is allowed.</li>
      <li><strong>Spam.</strong> Sending or relaying unsolicited bulk email or messages, or hosting pages that only exist to promote spam.</li>
      <li><strong>Abusive traffic generation.</strong> Running bots, scrapers, or load-testing tools that target systems you do not own.</li>
      <li><strong>Network scanning.</strong> Probing, scanning, or attacking other hosts from within a deployed container.</li>
      <li><strong>Circumventing resource limits.</strong> Attempting to exceed your quota through technical means, account duplication, or other workarounds.</li>
      <li><strong>Reselling access.</strong> Offering HelloDeploy capacity to third parties as a commercial service.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="resource-responsibility">Resource responsibility</h2>
    <p>Your application must operate within the limits described in the <a href="/service-limits">Service Limits</a> page. An application that puts other users at risk, for example by exhausting shared CPU, memory, or network capacity, may be stopped straight away to protect them. You are told afterwards and can appeal as described below.</p>

    <h2 id="account-rules">Account rules</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>One account per person. Creating multiple accounts to circumvent limits is prohibited.</li>
      <li>You are responsible for all activity under your account, including actions taken by project team members you invite.</li>
      <li>Do not share your account credentials.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="enforcement">Enforcement</h2>
    <p>Violations are handled progressively:</p>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Warning</strong> — notification by email for a first or minor violation.</li>
      <li><strong>Suspension</strong> — account access suspended while the violation is reviewed.</li>
      <li><strong>Termination</strong> — account and all associated data permanently removed for serious or repeat violations.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>Severe violations (malware, illegal content, active attacks) may result in immediate suspension or termination without a prior warning.</p>
    <p>When we act, we tell you which rule was broken and what you can do to fix it, unless doing so would help an ongoing attack or break the law. We keep a record of each enforcement action and its reason.</p>

    <h3 id="appeals">Appeals</h3>
    <p>If you think an action was a mistake, email <a href="mailto:<%= legalContactEmail %>"><%= legalContactEmail %></a> with your account email, the affected project, and why you think the decision should change. A person reviews every appeal, and we reply with the outcome. Do not include passwords, tokens, or secret values in your email.</p>

    <h2 id="reporting">Reporting</h2>
    <p>If you believe another user is violating this policy, contact the platform administrator at <a href="mailto:<%= legalContactEmail %>"><%= legalContactEmail %></a>.</p>
  </article>
</div>

<%- include('../partials/legal/footer') %>
